'''Tarsiriel''' (天使メガミエル, ''Tenshi Megamieru'', '''Angel Megamiel''') is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of [[LeMurr]] introduced in [[Stratospheric Pathway]]. They were added in [[Version 13.2 Update|Version 13.2]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Tarsiriel
|image = E 680.png
|first appearance = '''ZL''': [[Prairie Harbor|Sub-chapter 10 - Prairie Harbor]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Cheerful Heretic|Sub-chapter 17 - Cheerful Heretic]]
|money drop = 750¢ - 2,962¢
}}

==Enemy==
Tarsiriel is similar to [[Loris]], albeit with higher health but a notably shorter standing range and Long Distance reach. However, this enemy can be more problematic by Slowing instead of Cursing, giving them some similarity to [[Croakley]]. The similarity also extends to a 100% chance to effectively perma-slow, though the [[Ototo Corps|Slow Beam Style]] can bring the uptime under 100%.

==Strategy==
Due to Tarsiriel's Long Distance specifications, they can only attack when a Cat is already in Tarsiriel's blind spot or Tarsiriel is in position to snipe the [[Cat Base]]. As such, they're easy to handle when alone, but can be a problem when backing tough frontline and midrange enemies. This, as well as their Sage type, makes [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control options]] rather ineffective unless the crowd-control unit happens to be an [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel]] [[:Category:Sage Slayer Cats|Sage Slayer]], such as [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Catcrates]]. That aside, speedy or [[:Category:Cats with Slow Immunity|slow-immune Cats]] are optimal for getting inside the blind spot and avoiding the perma-slow.

Since Tarsiriel's Sage type keeps them from being pushed far by knockback effects, firing the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] to push non-Sage enemies behind Tarsiriel is a good way to leave them open to attack.

