==Trivia==
*Tarsiriel's name is a combination of ''[[wikipedia:Tarsier|tarsier]]'' (a nocturnal primate with big eyes and long hind limbs) and ''El'' (the Hebrew word for God, commonly used as a suffix in angel names).
*Tarsiriel's Japanese name, Megamiel (メガミエル ''Megamieru''), is a combination of 目が見える ''megamieru'' (to be able to see), 眼鏡 ''megane'' (glasses), 眼鏡猿 ''meganezaru'' (tarsier), ''El'' and possibly 女神 ''megami'' (goddess).
*Since many [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sages]] are based on historical figures and Tarsiriel debuts in [[Stratospheric Pathway]], an American-themed sub-chapter, Tarsiriel may be based on an American historical figure. The focus given to their glasses might allude to [[wikipedia:Benjamin Franklin|Benjamin Franklin]], a Founding Father who invented bifocals, while the closest known match for their design is [[wikipedia:Peter Cooper|Peter Cooper]], an inventor and industrialist best known for creating America's first steam locomotive, ''[[wikipedia:Tom Thumb (locomotive)|Tom Thumb]]''.
*Tarsiriel bears a slight resemblance to Brazilian educator and philosopher [[wikipedia:Paulo Freire|Paulo Freire]].
*Tarsiriel's description and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/Sage typing may reference [[wikipedia:Saint Peter|St. Peter]], an Apostle of Jesus whose name means "stone"; St. Peter is often portrayed as Heaven's gatekeeper and greeter awaiting those who reach the [[wikipedia:Pearly gates|pearly gates]], as he was promised the [[wikipedia:Keys of Heaven|Keys of Heaven]] in the Bible.

